    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "8ac0f8716137c1d3497fbf0d18cc39eb",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"spike-short-model-lab\">Spike Short Model Lab</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Which trades will be <strong>continuation losers</strong> (net <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\le -200||)</marimo-tex> bps)? About 15% of baseline trades lose that much and\nthey make up 60\u201368% of all losing bps. Each model below scores <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(P(\\text{tail loser})||)</marimo-tex> for a trade from facts known\nwhen the short would be placed (the arm bar has closed, entry is the next open), and a trade is skipped when the\nscore crosses a threshold.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Protocol.</strong> Models, calibration and thresholds are all set on <strong>Jul 2025 \u2013 Jun 2026</strong> using out-of-fold scores\n(blocked time folds with a 5-day purge). <strong>Q3 2026</strong> and <strong>Oct \u2013 Nov 2026</strong> are scored once with everything frozen.\nThe tune row in the tables is out-of-fold, so it is a fair estimate too. Targets: win rate 60\u201370%, profit factor <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\ge 1.5||)</marimo-tex>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
